/android/app/release
.env
*.key
# Release signing — MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED.
#
# The upload keystore and its passwords are what prove a build came from us.
# Anyone holding both can sign an APK that Android and the Play Store will
# accept as a genuine Karde update. They are not recoverable if lost, either:
# a replacement keystore means the app can no longer be updated in place.
#
# Neither file has ever been committed. Keep it that way — back them up
# somewhere private instead.
android/key.properties
android/upload-keystore.jks
*.jks
*.keystore

# Obfuscation symbol files. Archived per release out-of-band; without them a
# release's crash reports cannot be decoded, but they do not belong in the repo.
/build/debug-info/

# Internal working notes and one-off audit output — kept locally, not published.
CONTEXT_INFO.md
PUBLISH_CHECKLIST.md
PLAY_STORE_GUIDE.md
TEST_PLAN.md
TEST_PLAN_i18n.md
